---
import BaseCrisp from "../layouts/BaseCrisp.astro";

// one green check, reused across pricing lists
const check = `<svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M3 8.5l3 3 7-7" stroke="#1f9d64" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>`;
const play = `<svg width="20" height="24" viewBox="0 0 26 30" fill="#fff" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M0 0 L26 15 L0 30 Z"/></svg>`;
---

<BaseCrisp>
  {/* ===== Hero ===== */}
  <section class="hero"><div class="wrap">
    <span class="pill"><span class="t">OPEN SOURCE</span> self-host · your keys · 0% markup</span>
    <h1>The flight recorder<br><span class="thin">for AI agents.</span></h1>
    <p class="hsub">Autonomous agents fail without crashing — a clean 200, well-formed tokens, and the run already three steps off course. Tracelane records every run to a tamper-evident ledger you can prove.</p>
    <div class="hcta"><a href="#notify" class="btn btn-lava">Be first to know →</a><a href="https://github.com/tracelane" rel="me noopener" class="btn btn-ghost">GitHub</a></div>
    <div class="hmicro">apache-2.0 core · self-host anywhere · no credit card</div>

    {/* Hero video stage — drop /hero.mp4 + /hero-poster.jpg; overlay shows until then */}
    <div class="stage-wrap reveal">
      <div class="win-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="addr">tracelane — replay</span></div>
      <div class="stage" id="hero-stage">
        <video id="hero-video" class="stage-video" poster="/hero-poster.jpg" preload="none" playsinline controls style="display:none">
          <source src="/hero.mp4" type="video/mp4" />
        </video>
        <button class="stage-overlay" id="hero-play" type="button" aria-label="Play the tracelane story">
          <span class="play" set:html={play} />
          <span class="cap">Watch a run recorded, replayed, and verified</span>
        </button>
      </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div></section>

  {/* ===== Keyword pillars — the spine (re-skinned Record / Replay / Prove) ===== */}
  <section id="pillars" style="padding:0 0 44px"><div class="wrap">
    <div class="pillars reveal">
      <div class="pillar"><div class="kw"><span class="dot"></span>Gateway</div><p>One endpoint in front of every model. Your keys, 0% markup, bounded overhead — every call captured in full fidelity.</p></div>
      <div class="pillar"><div class="kw"><span class="dot"></span>Observability</div><p>Step-level traces — every prompt, tool call, latency and cost, down to the exact call that broke.</p></div>
      <div class="pillar"><div class="kw"><span class="dot"></span>Audit</div><p>A tamper-evident, Ed25519-signed ledger. Verify the whole chain yourself, offline.</p></div>
    </div>
  </div></section>

  {/* ===== Provider marquee ===== */}
  <div class="marquee"><div class="wrap mrow">
    <span>OpenAI</span><span>Anthropic</span><span>Google</span><span>Mistral</span><span>Bedrock</span><span>Groq</span><b>30+ providers</b>
  </div></div>

  {/* ===== Problem trio ===== */}
  <section><div class="wrap center">
    <div class="eyebrow">Why agent failures stay invisible</div>
    <div class="stitle">A clean 200 tells you nothing.</div>
    <div class="trio reveal">
      <div class="tcard"><div class="tn">01</div><h4>State drift compounds</h4><p>A bad tool output at step 2 corrupts every step after it. The model keeps going, confidently, further from the goal.</p></div>
      <div class="tcard"><div class="tn">02</div><h4>Success codes lie</h4><p>A 200 and clean tokens say nothing about whether the state is still valid three steps later. Tracelane reconstructs the causal path, not the request log.</p></div>
      <div class="tcard"><div class="tn">03</div><h4>Tools run code</h4><p>Every tool call executes on your behalf. The ledger is the cryptographic record of exactly what ran.</p></div>
    </div>
  </div></section>

  {/* ===== Signature verify block ===== */}
  <section style="padding-top:0"><div class="wrap">
    <div class="verify reveal">
      <div class="eyebrow">Independently verifiable</div>
      <h2>You don't trust us. You verify us.</h2>
      <p class="vs">SHA-256 hash chain, Ed25519-signed every 100 events. Anchored batches carry a resolved Sigstore Rekor v2 inclusion proof (best-effort; universal per-run anchoring on the roadmap). Tampering means breaking the math — not editing a row.</p>
      <div class="vterm">
        <div><span class="p">$</span> <span class="c">tlane verify &lt;trace-id&gt;</span></div>
        <div><span class="ok">✓</span> <span class="c">signature valid</span> <span class="p">(Ed25519, Merkle root)</span></div>
        <div><span class="ok">✓</span> <span class="c">hash chain unbroken</span> <span class="p">(SHA-256)</span></div>
        <div><span class="ok">✓</span> <span class="c">tamper-evident: yes</span><span class="cursor"></span></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </header>

  {/* ===== Why agent failures stay invisible ===== */}
  <section id="why" class="container py-24 border-t border-border">
    <div class="reveal max-w-2xl">
      <h2 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-fg">Why agent failures stay invisible</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="mt-16 grid gap-5 md:grid-cols-3 reveal-group cards-hover">
      <article class="glass rounded-2xl p-8">
        <p class="text-fg-muted leading-relaxed"><span class="text-fg font-medium">State drift compounds.</span> A bad tool output at step 2 corrupts every step after it. The model keeps going, confidently, further from the goal.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="glass rounded-2xl p-8">
        <p class="text-fg-muted leading-relaxed"><span class="text-fg font-medium">Success codes lie.</span> A 200 and clean tokens say nothing about whether the state is still valid three steps later. Tracelane reconstructs the causal path, not just the request log.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="glass rounded-2xl p-8">
        <p class="text-fg-muted leading-relaxed"><span class="text-fg font-medium">Tools are an open execution surface.</span> Every tool call is code running on your behalf. The ledger is the cryptographic record of exactly what ran.</p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  {/* ===== Record / Replay / Prove ===== */}
  <section id="what" class="container py-24 border-t border-border">
    <div class="reveal max-w-2xl">
      <h2 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-fg">Everything your agent does, on the record.</h2>
      <p class="mt-4 text-lg text-fg-muted">Three things, one Rust binary. Open core. Apache 2.0.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="mt-16 grid gap-5 md:grid-cols-6 md:auto-rows-fr reveal-group cards-hover">
      <article class="glass rounded-2xl p-6 md:col-span-3 md:row-span-2 flex flex-col">
        <div class="feat-glyph" aria-hidden="true"><span class="glyph-eq"><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i></span></div>
        <p class="font-mono text-xs text-pop mb-4 lowercase tracking-wider">01 — record</p>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-medium text-fg">Universal gateway</h3>
        <p class="mt-3 text-fg-muted leading-relaxed">
          One endpoint in front of every model. Bring your own keys, 0% markup, bounded overhead — and every call is captured in full fidelity.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article class="glass rounded-2xl p-6 md:col-span-3">
        <div class="feat-glyph" aria-hidden="true"><svg class="glyph-replay" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M21 12a9 9 0 1 1-2.64-6.36"/><path d="M21 3v5h-5"/></svg></div>
        <p class="font-mono text-xs text-pop mb-4 lowercase tracking-wider">02 — replay</p>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-medium text-fg">Replay the failure</h3>
        <p class="mt-3 text-fg-muted leading-relaxed">
          Step-level trace of prompts, tool calls, latency, and cost — down to the exact call that broke, and whether you've seen it before.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article class="glass rounded-2xl p-6 md:col-span-3">
        <div class="feat-glyph" aria-hidden="true"><svg class="glyph-prove" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.4" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M4 12.5l5 5L20 6"/></svg></div>
        <p class="font-mono text-xs text-pop mb-4 lowercase tracking-wider">03 — prove</p>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-medium text-fg">Prove it</h3>
        <p class="mt-3 text-fg-muted leading-relaxed">
          A tamper-evident ledger — SHA-256 hash chain, Ed25519-signed Merkle root — anyone can verify offline. Logs you can't argue with.
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  {/* ===== Migration ===== */}
  <section id="migrate" class="container py-24 border-t border-border">
    <div class="reveal max-w-2xl">
      <h2 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-fg">Migrating from a tool that got acquired or breached?</h2>
      <p class="mt-4 text-lg text-fg-muted">Migration is forward re-instrumentation: we rewrite your config and SDK wiring to point at Tracelane. No data leaves your infrastructure, and your history stays where it is.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="mt-12 grid gap-6 md:grid-cols-2 reveal-group cards-hover">
      <article class="glass rounded-2xl p-8">
        <h3 class="text-xl font-medium text-fg">From Helicone</h3>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-fg-muted">For teams moving off Helicone.</p>
        <p class="mt-4 text-sm text-fg-muted"><span class="text-fg">tlane migrate helicone</span> rewrites your <span class="text-fg">HELICONE_*</span> env vars, Helicone base URLs, and custom headers to their Tracelane equivalents across your source tree — printed as a diff, dry-run by default. New runs land in Tracelane the moment you apply it; historical traces stay in Helicone.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="glass rounded-2xl p-8">
        <h3 class="text-xl font-medium text-fg">From LiteLLM</h3>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-fg-muted">A Rust request path with signed releases and attested provenance.</p>
        <p class="mt-4 text-sm text-fg-muted">Drop-in gateway replacement; <span class="text-fg">tlane import-litellm</span> reads your <span class="text-fg">litellm_config.yaml</span> and emits the equivalent Tracelane config. Sigstore-signed releases, attested build provenance, Trusted Publishing OIDC — no long-lived registry tokens.</p>
      </article>
  </div></section>

  {/* ===== Migration ===== */}
  <section id="migrate"><div class="wrap">
    <div class="eyebrow">Migration</div>
    <div class="stitle">Coming from a tool that got acquired or breached?</div>
    <p class="lead" style="margin-left:0;text-align:left">Importers land with V1 — no data leaves your infrastructure during migration.</p>
    <div class="grid2 reveal">
      <div class="tcard"><h4>From Helicone</h4><p style="margin-top:8px">For teams on Helicone after it entered maintenance mode (Mintlify acquisition, Mar 2026). One-command import of traces, configs, prompts, and rate-limit rules — lands with V1.</p></div>
      <div class="tcard"><h4>From LiteLLM</h4><p style="margin-top:8px">After CVE-2026-33634 (Mar 24) and CVE-2026-42208 (Apr 24). Drop-in gateway replacement; config import lands with V1. Sigstore-signed releases, SLSA Build L3 provenance, Trusted Publishing OIDC — no long-lived tokens.</p></div>
    </div>
  </div></section>

  {/* ===== Audit ledger ===== */}
  <section id="audit" class="container py-24 border-t border-border relative overflow-hidden">
    <div class="glow glow-teal" style="width:520px;height:420px;right:-80px;top:40px"></div>
    <div class="relative z-[2]">
      <p class="font-mono text-xs text-pop mb-4 tracking-wider lowercase">the audit ledger</p>
      <h2 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl md:text-5xl font-semibold tracking-tight max-w-3xl text-fg leading-[1.05]">
        Every run. On the record. <span class="grad-text">Provably.</span>
      </h2>
      <p class="mt-6 text-lg text-fg-muted max-w-2xl leading-relaxed">
        Each event is hash-chained with SHA-256. Every 100 events, the Merkle root is signed with Ed25519. Verify the whole chain offline — tampering means breaking SHA-256 or forging a signature, not editing a row.
      </p>

      <div class="mt-16 grid gap-5 md:grid-cols-3 text-sm reveal-group cards-hover">
        <div class="glass rounded-2xl p-6">
          <p class="font-mono text-xs text-fg-dim lowercase tracking-wider">eu ai act</p>
          <p class="mt-3 text-fg-muted">Article 12 export pack — full audit trail for high-risk AI systems. Annex III enforcement provisionally deferred to Dec 2, 2027 (Digital Omnibus political agreement, May 7, 2026; pending formal adoption — <a href="https://www.whitecase.com/insight-alert/eu-agrees-digital-omnibus-deal-simplify-ai-rules" class="underline decoration-fg-subtle hover:decoration-fg transition-colors" rel="noopener">details</a>); the ledger is available today.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="glass rounded-2xl p-6">
          <p class="font-mono text-xs text-fg-dim lowercase tracking-wider">india dpdp</p>
          <p class="mt-3 text-fg-muted">Phase II enforcement Nov 13, 2026. Tracelane enforces no per-tenant storage region today; region pinning is on the roadmap. The audit ledger has no expiry clock — it is kept for the life of the ledger.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="glass rounded-2xl p-6">
          <p class="font-mono text-xs text-fg-dim lowercase tracking-wider">hipaa</p>
          <p class="mt-3 text-fg-muted">BAA available on Business tier. PII redaction inline. Provider keys envelope-encrypted.</p>
        </div>
  <section id="audit" style="padding-top:0"><div class="wrap">
    <div class="eyebrow">The audit ledger</div>
    <div class="stitle">Every run. On the record. Provably.</div>
    <p class="lead" style="margin-left:0;text-align:left;max-width:640px">Each event is hash-chained with SHA-256. Every 100 events the Merkle root is signed with Ed25519. Verify the whole chain offline — tampering means breaking SHA-256 or forging a signature, not editing a row.</p>
    <div class="grid3-cards reveal">
      <div class="mini"><div class="k">eu ai act</div><p>Article 12 export pack — full audit trail for high-risk AI systems. Annex III enforcement provisionally deferred to Dec 2, 2027 (Digital Omnibus political agreement, May 7, 2026; pending formal adoption — <a href="https://www.whitecase.com/insight-alert/eu-agrees-digital-omnibus-deal-simplify-ai-rules" rel="noopener">details</a>); the ledger ships at V1.</p></div>
      <div class="mini"><div class="k">india dpdp</div><p>Phase II enforcement Nov 13, 2026. EU data residency at V1; India residency on the roadmap, on demand. Audit-log retention configurable.</p></div>
      <div class="mini"><div class="k">hipaa</div><p>BAA available on Business tier. PII redaction inline. Provider keys envelope-encrypted.</p></div>
    </div>
  </div></section>

  {/* ===== Dev / code ===== */}
  <section style="padding-top:0"><div class="wrap dev">
    <div>
      <div class="eyebrow">For developers</div>
      <h2>One line.<br>Every provider.</h2>
      <p>Point any OpenAI-compatible client at Tracelane. Your code doesn't change.</p>
      <a href="/docs" class="btn btn-lava">Read the docs →</a>
      <div class="dstats">
        <div class="dstat"><div class="n">30+</div><div class="l">providers</div></div>
