  <section id="faq" class="container py-24 border-t border-border">
    <h2 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-fg text-center">Frequently asked.</h2>
    <div class="mt-16 space-y-4 max-w-3xl mx-auto reveal-group text-left">
      <details class="glass rounded-2xl px-6 py-5 group">
        <summary class="cursor-pointer font-medium text-lg flex items-center justify-between text-fg">What is Tracelane?<span class="text-fg-dim group-open:rotate-45 transition-transform">+</span></summary>
        <p class="mt-4 text-fg-muted leading-relaxed">Tracelane is an open-source (Apache 2.0) flight recorder for AI agents: a universal Rust LLM gateway, full-fidelity OpenTelemetry observability, and a tamper-evident audit ledger. Each event is SHA-256 hash-chained and the Merkle root is Ed25519-signed every 100 events, so any trace can be verified offline.</p>
      </details>

      <details class="glass rounded-2xl px-6 py-5 group">
        <summary class="cursor-pointer font-medium text-lg flex items-center justify-between text-fg">How is Tracelane different from Helicone, LangSmith, or Langfuse?<span class="text-fg-dim group-open:rotate-45 transition-transform">+</span></summary>
        <p class="mt-4 text-fg-muted leading-relaxed">Tracelane unifies the gateway, observability, pre-flight policy, and a tamper-evident audit ledger in one Rust binary. Helicone, Langfuse, and LangSmith are observability-first — you bring your own gateway and your own guardrails. Tracelane is Apache 2.0 core with a published self-host path; Helicone's gateway is GPL-3.0 (corporate-procurement-hostile), Arize Phoenix is ELv2 (no SaaS resale), and LangSmith is closed-source. The audit ledger is hash-chained and Ed25519-signed — no competitor in this category offers cryptographic audit-log integrity at the trace level.</p>
      </details>

      <details class="glass rounded-2xl px-6 py-5 group">
        <summary class="cursor-pointer font-medium text-lg flex items-center justify-between text-fg">What about LangSmith Engine?<span class="text-fg-dim group-open:rotate-45 transition-transform">+</span></summary>
        <p class="mt-4 text-fg-muted leading-relaxed">LangSmith Engine (May 13, 2026) clusters production failures after they happen and drafts pull requests to fix them. Tracelane's pre-flight policy checks flag failure modes at the gateway before the call reaches the provider —. Engine is locked to the LangSmith trace surface and LangChain-managed inference keys per LangChain's terms of service; Tracelane is neutral OTel ingest with 0% BYOK markup across 30+ providers. Different layer of the agent reliability stack. <a href="/vs/langsmith-engine" class="underline decoration-fg-subtle hover:decoration-fg transition-colors">Detailed comparison →</a></p>
      </details>

      <details class="glass rounded-2xl px-6 py-5 group">
        <summary class="cursor-pointer font-medium text-lg flex items-center justify-between text-fg">Is Tracelane really open source?<span class="text-fg-dim group-open:rotate-45 transition-transform">+</span></summary>
        <p class="mt-4 text-fg-muted leading-relaxed">Yes. The core (Rust gateway, ingest workers, observability backend, pre-flight layer, CLI, SDKs, audit verifiers) is Apache 2.0. The <code class="font-mono text-sm">/spec</code> directory is CC0. Paid features are gated by the workspace_entitlements table at the application layer, not by a license-string compare.</p>
      </details>

      <details class="glass rounded-2xl px-6 py-5 group">
        <summary class="cursor-pointer font-medium text-lg flex items-center justify-between text-fg">Which providers does Tracelane support?<span class="text-fg-dim group-open:rotate-45 transition-transform">+</span></summary>
        <p class="mt-4 text-fg-muted leading-relaxed">30+ providers today — 7 native adapters (Anthropic, OpenAI, Google Gemini, Google Vertex, AWS Bedrock, Azure OpenAI, Cohere) plus any OpenAI-compatible endpoint, including Together, Fireworks, Groq, OpenRouter, DeepSeek, xAI, and Mistral. One canonical wire format across all of them.</p>
      </details>

      <details class="glass rounded-2xl px-6 py-5 group">
        <summary class="cursor-pointer font-medium text-lg flex items-center justify-between text-fg">Does Tracelane support EU AI Act Article 12?<span class="text-fg-dim group-open:rotate-45 transition-transform">+</span></summary>
        <p class="mt-4 text-fg-muted leading-relaxed">The Tamper-Evident Agent Ledger is a $999/mo add-on, available on any plan. The audit ledger (SHA-256 hash chain, Ed25519-signed Merkle root), and an Article 12 documentation pack are available today. Tracelane enforces no per-tenant storage region, signs no BAA, and makes no regulatory-conformance claim (the Business tier; India residency on demand). EU AI Act Annex III obligations were originally scheduled for Aug 2, 2026; the Digital Omnibus political agreement (May 7, 2026) provisionally deferred enforcement to Dec 2, 2027, pending formal adoption (<a href="https://www.whitecase.com/insight-alert/eu-agrees-digital-omnibus-deal-simplify-ai-rules" class="underline decoration-fg-subtle hover:decoration-fg transition-colors" rel="noopener">details</a>). The ledger ships now so regulated buyers can build audit history before binding enforcement.</p>
      </details>

      <details class="glass rounded-2xl px-6 py-5 group">
        <summary class="cursor-pointer font-medium text-lg flex items-center justify-between text-fg">What's the latency overhead?<span class="text-fg-dim group-open:rotate-45 transition-transform">+</span></summary>
        <p class="mt-4 text-fg-muted leading-relaxed">Gateway overhead targets p50 &lt;5ms, p95 &lt;15ms, p99 &lt;25ms (excluding provider time). Pre-flight policy layer targets p99 &lt;50ms on commodity CPU. These are engineering targets — measured numbers will publish as the Tracelane Reliability Benchmark v1.0.</p>
      </details>

      <details class="glass rounded-2xl px-6 py-5 group">
        <summary class="cursor-pointer font-medium text-lg flex items-center justify-between text-fg">Can I self-host?<span class="text-fg-dim group-open:rotate-45 transition-transform">+</span></summary>
        <p class="mt-4 text-fg-muted leading-relaxed">Yes. Docker Compose for development, Helm chart for production. The full ClickHouse + R2 stack runs on a single small Hetzner node. See the <a href="https://docs.tracelane.dev/self-hosting" class="underline decoration-fg-subtle hover:decoration-fg transition-colors" rel="noopener">self-hosting guide</a>.</p>
      </details>

      <details class="glass rounded-2xl px-6 py-5 group">
        <summary class="cursor-pointer font-medium text-lg flex items-center justify-between text-fg">Is Tracelane available now?<span class="text-fg-dim group-open:rotate-45 transition-transform">+</span></summary>
        <p class="mt-4 text-fg-muted leading-relaxed">Yes — V1 is live. Start free at <a href="https://app.tracelane.dev/sign-in" class="underline decoration-fg-subtle hover:decoration-fg transition-colors">app.tracelane.dev</a>, or self-host the Apache 2.0 core. Sign up for product updates above if you want to hear when something ships.</p>
      </details>
    </div>
  </section>

